cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this library, please cite this repository as below, and cite the
  original authors of each classical result it builds on, named in the README
  of lean-classical-upstream.
title: >-
  lean-elementary-cellular-automata: growth, columns, rays and the erasure of
  local perturbations in the elementary cellular automata, machine-checked in
  Lean 4
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Palamarchuk
    given-names: Mykola
    email: lividgreen@gmail.com
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0007-2106-5777
    affiliation: Independent researcher
repository-code: https://github.com/lividgreen/lean-elementary-cellular-automata
url: https://lividgreen.github.io/lean-elementary-cellular-automata/
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 + Mathlib library on the 256 elementary cellular automata: the
  merge quotient of an update and the width of its reachability preorder, and
  the growing width decided at every quiescent rule — zero at every time or
  unbounded, unbounded at exactly 54 of the 128 — over the Wolfram number; the
  columns, windows and rays of an orbit that are eventually periodic; rule
  90's rays from a single cell at every rational speed; the erasure of a
  perturbation of two cells at every scale over a class of rules; and a
  bracket on which rules reproduce a pattern. No sorry, no native_decide,
  standard axioms only, with
  each capstone's axiom footprint asserted by a build-enforced guard.
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formal verification
  - cellular automata
  - elementary cellular automata
  - rule 90
  - symbolic dynamics
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23275249
# Deliberately only the concept DOI (decision 2026-07-28, as in the companion
# packages): per-version DOIs are minted after the tag, so an in-repo list is
# always one behind; Zenodo's record lists every version, and the concept DOI
# resolves to the latest.
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23275249
    description: >-
      Concept DOI — resolves to the latest archived version, and its Zenodo
      record lists the per-version DOIs.
